Detailed Resource Analysis1. Food Composition Table for Pakistan (FAO / Government of Pakistan)Resource Link: FAO Food Composition Table for PakistanWhat It Is: An official, comprehensive nutritional handbook published by the Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) in collaboration with the Pakistani government. It provides macronutrient, micronutrient, and caloric breakdowns for raw, cooked, and traditional food items across Pakistan.Why It Is Used: Standard international nutrition databases frequently lack accurate data for regional South Asian dishes (e.g., specific varieties of roti, regional dal preparations, localized meat dishes, and traditional sweets).Significance: Ensures that caloric calculation, portion estimation, and macro breakdowns reflect accurate local cooking methods, ingredient profiles, and regional diets.2. Food-Based Dietary Guidelines for Pakistan (Ministry of NHSR&C / FAO)Resource Link: FBDG Pakistan GuidelinesWhat It Is: National policy guidelines published by the Ministry of National Health Services, Regulations & Coordination in partnership with the FAO, outlining population-level dietary targets, food group categorizations, and healthy eating patterns tailored to regional health needs.Why It Is Used: Provides foundational rules for generating culturally appropriate meal plans and dietary advice that align with recognized national health standards.Significance: Prevents the AI from recommending non-viable or culturally inappropriate diets, ensuring all meal recommendations adhere to national dietary framework standards.3. WHO Guidelines on Physical Activity and Sedentary BehaviourResource Link: WHO Guidelines (2020)What It Is: The World Health Organization's peer-reviewed clinical guidelines establishing evidence-based recommendations on physical activity duration, intensity, resistance training, and sedentary behavior management across different age groups and medical conditions.Why It Is Used: Establishes a medical and public health baseline for exercise intensity, safe progression rates, and weekly activity targets.Significance: Prevents unsafe, extreme, or non-scientifically validated fitness routines by grounding generated workout plans in WHO clinical safety standards.4. USDA FoodData Central DatasetsResource Link: USDA FoodData Central DownloadsWhat It Is: An open-access nutrition database managed by the United States Department of Agriculture containing comprehensive chemical analyses, raw ingredient data, and commercial packaged food entries.Why It Is Used: Serves as a reference dataset for standardized global food products, raw commodity ingredients, and detailed micronutrient metrics (e.g., amino acid profiles, trace minerals).Significance: Broadens the system's coverage beyond regional recipes, allowing the RAG pipeline to accurately identify imported goods, commercial packaged items, and generic single-ingredient foods.5. Pakistan Dietary Nutrition Report 2019 (Planning Commission of Pakistan)Resource Link: Pakistan Dietary Nutrition Report 2019What It Is: A research report published by the Planning Commission of Pakistan detailing nutritional intake statistics, widespread micronutrient deficiencies (e.g., Vitamin D, Iron, Zinc), and public health risk factors across the country.Why It Is Used: Provides context on prevalent regional health issues and dietary gaps.Significance: Enables the LLM to deliver context-aware health suggestions—such as proactively emphasizing iron-rich or vitamin-D-dense local foods when users express relevant wellness goals or symptoms.4. End-to-End Data Flow1. User Query (Text / Voice via Retell AI)
   └── Received by FastAPI Backend

2. RAG Retrieval Phase
   ├── Query converted to dense vector via BAAI/bge-base-en-v1.5
   └── ChromaDB returns top-k matching document chunks from indexed PDFs/CSVs

3. Context Augmentation
   └── Retrieved local nutritional data & clinical rules merged into LLM Prompt

4. Generation Phase
   └── Groq API runs openai/gpt-oss-120b to produce grounding-checked response

5. Output Phase
   └── Formatted JSON/Text returned to Flutter App (or spoken back via Retell AI)